{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The retrieval-evaluation corpus: a fixed set of documents whose only job is",
    "to be chunked and searched the same way every run. Document text lives in",
    "eval-corpus/, one Markdown file each -- see eval-corpus/README.md for why none of",
    "it is copied from a real document.",
    "",
    "Grants decide who can retrieve what, and retrieval filters before it ranks, so the",
    "spread here is deliberate: alice (finance) and bob (exec) see overlapping but",
    "different subsets, the channel sees only team-granted documents, and the transition",
    "report is granted to one person so no channel can reach it."
  ],
